  Breadcrumbs \n\nHistory for \n\n  1. <::after> [ haproxy ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits)\n  2. <::after> [ src ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits/master/src)\n  3. [ tools.c ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits/master/src/tools.c)\n\n\n\non  [ master ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/master)\n\n##  User selector \n\nAll users \n\n##  Datepicker \n\nAll time \n\n##  Commit history \n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Aug 3, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ BUILD: tools: fix C23 incompatible strrchr usage ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/8745931e6f1f7f7010de2a7a2ab430b398755f6c \"BUILD: tools: fix C23 incompatible strrchr usage\n\nFix the following warning by ensuring strrchr\\(\\) return type is set to\n'const char *' if its input is declared as such.\n\nsrc/tools.c: In function \u2018str2net\u2019:\nsrc/tools.c:1618:16: error: assignment discards \u2018const\u2019 qualifier from pointer target type \\[-Werror=discarded-qualifiers\\]\n 1618 |         if \\(\\(c = strrchr\\(str, '/'\\)\\) != NULL\\) {\n      |                ^\n\nThis build warning was introduced by the following patch.\n\n  9bc6c4d18c2ea9836c171977c1c7c2979ecbb132\n  OPTIM: tools/str2net: only duplicate the string when a slash is present\n\nThis change is required since C23, as strrchr\\(\\), along other functions\nwhich accept a const-qualified pointer without returning a const type\nare now declared as macro with generics to preserve the const qualifier.\n\nSee https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n3020.pdf for\ndetails.\n\nNo need to backport, unless the above patch is.\")\n\nShow description for 8745931 \n\n[ ](/a-denoyelle) [ a-denoyelle ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=a-denoyelle)\n\ncommitted  yesterday \n\n\u00b7 \n\n39 / 39 \n\n[ 8745931  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/8745931e6f1f7f7010de2a7a2ab430b398755f6c)\n\nCopy full SHA for 8745931 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/8745931e6f1f7f7010de2a7a2ab430b398755f6c/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/8745931e6f1f7f7010de2a7a2ab430b398755f6c)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ OPTIM: tools/str2net: only duplicate the string when a slash is present ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/9bc6c4d18c2ea9836c171977c1c7c2979ecbb132 \"OPTIM: tools/str2net: only duplicate the string when a slash is present\n\nThe str2net\\(\\) and str62net\\(\\) functions systematically strdup\\(\\) the\ninput pattern before parsing it, while this is only needed when a '/'\nis present. Given that this '/' is already looked up, better move the\nallocation inside that block so that no allocation is performed when\nnone is present.\n\nDoing so saves ~5% load time on plain IPv4 addresses and ~8% on plain\nIPv6 addresses, while not changing anything for addresses with masks.\")\n\nShow description for 9bc6c4d \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  yesterday \n\n\u00b7 \n\n39 / 39 \n\n[ 9bc6c4d  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/9bc6c4d18c2ea9836c171977c1c7c2979ecbb132)\n\nCopy full SHA for 9bc6c4d \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/9bc6c4d18c2ea9836c171977c1c7c2979ecbb132/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/9bc6c4d18c2ea9836c171977c1c7c2979ecbb132)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Jul 28, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ BUG/MEDIUM: tools: make string encoding possible to fail instead of truncating ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/b947f6075542030160a35d7f8c25beaa1c0e7584 \"BUG/MEDIUM: tools: make string encoding possible to fail instead of truncating\n\nencode_string\\(\\) and encode_chunk\\(\\) functions were silently truncated the\noutput string if it is too small. encode_string\\(\\) is not used but\nencode_chunk\\(\\) is used to encode urls \\(url_enc converter and ocsp\\). In this\ncontext it is not expected to have an url partially encoded.\n\nSo let's slightly change the API to add an extra argument to these functions\nto be able to fail when the output string is too small. <truncate> must be\nset to 0 to return an error \\(NULL\\) instead of truncate the output string.\n\nurl_enc converter and ocsp were also update to trigger an error in that\ncase.\n\nThe issue is pretty minor but it remains an API change, so it is tagged as\nMEDIUM. It could be backported to 3.4 and probably as far as 3.2 or 3.0.\")\n\nShow description for b947f60 \n\n[ ](/capflam) [ capflam ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=capflam)\n\ncommitted  last week \n\n[ b947f60  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/b947f6075542030160a35d7f8c25beaa1c0e7584)\n\nCopy full SHA for b947f60 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/b947f6075542030160a35d7f8c25beaa1c0e7584/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/b947f6075542030160a35d7f8c25beaa1c0e7584)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Jul 24, 2026 \n\n  * ####  \" class=\"color-fg-default\" href=\"/haproxy/haproxy/commit/34b9b528e83e864170a773c66afc0cbca687c475\" tabindex=\"-1\">OPTIM: tools: keep a cache of recent localtime() and gmtime() \n\nShow description for 34b9b52 \n\n[ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\nand \n\n[ zino7825 ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=zino7825)\n\ncommitted  2 weeks ago \n\n\u00b7 \n\n39 / 39 \n\n[ 34b9b52  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/34b9b528e83e864170a773c66afc0cbca687c475)\n\nCopy full SHA for 34b9b52 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/34b9b528e83e864170a773c66afc0cbca687c475/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/34b9b528e83e864170a773c66afc0cbca687c475)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Jul 2, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ BUG/MINOR: tools: fix invalid character detection in strl2ic() ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/c6d71297bcc6a9410d3cff46322f3c17f334b99e \"BUG/MINOR: tools: fix invalid character detection in strl2ic\\(\\)\n\nASCII characters with a value smaller than '0' were not properly\ndetected as invalid characters, leading to incorrect behavior. The\nstrl2irc\\(\\) and strl2llrc\\(\\) functions are not impacted because this\nsituation is detected by their overflow checks.\n\nFixes Github issue #3357.\")\n\nShow description for c6d7129 \n\n[ zhanhb ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=zhanhb)\n\nauthored and \n\n[ cognet ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=cognet)\n\ncommitted  on Jul 2 \n\n\u00b7 \n\n38 / 39 \n\n[ c6d7129  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/c6d71297bcc6a9410d3cff46322f3c17f334b99e)\n\nCopy full SHA for c6d7129 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/c6d71297bcc6a9410d3cff46322f3c17f334b99e/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/c6d71297bcc6a9410d3cff46322f3c17f334b99e)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Jun 1, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ MINOR: debug: add -dA to dump an archive of all dependencies ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/030a2bfeeb004862ce6b38a4964357e71a709ffa \"MINOR: debug: add -dA to dump an archive of all dependencies\n\nThis adds \")\n\nShow description for 030a2bf \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Jun 1 \n\n\u00b7 \n\n39 / 39 \n\n[ 030a2bf  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/030a2bfeeb004862ce6b38a4964357e71a709ffa)\n\nCopy full SHA for 030a2bf \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/030a2bfeeb004862ce6b38a4964357e71a709ffa/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/030a2bfeeb004862ce6b38a4964357e71a709ffa)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ MINOR: deinit: release the in-memory copy of shared libs ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/f8fd6d25d8d12035f7f810470ac6a6a30c0aa34e \"MINOR: deinit: release the in-memory copy of shared libs\n\nWhen shared libs were loaded via \")\n\nShow description for f8fd6d2 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Jun 1 \n\n[ f8fd6d2  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/f8fd6d25d8d12035f7f810470ac6a6a30c0aa34e)\n\nCopy full SHA for f8fd6d2 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/f8fd6d25d8d12035f7f810470ac6a6a30c0aa34e/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/f8fd6d25d8d12035f7f810470ac6a6a30c0aa34e)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on May 26, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ MEDIUM: tools: switch the main PRNG to a thread-local xoshiro256** ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/4a9ec66fd89cc55521e6dac42d881b435b95b50c \"MEDIUM: tools: switch the main PRNG to a thread-local xoshiro256**\n\nThe current PRNG is xoroshiro128**, it was introduced in 2.2 with\ncommit 52bf83939 \\(\")\n\nShow description for 4a9ec66 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on May 26 \n\n\u00b7 \n\n1 / 1 \n\n[ 4a9ec66  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/4a9ec66fd89cc55521e6dac42d881b435b95b50c)\n\nCopy full SHA for 4a9ec66 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/4a9ec66fd89cc55521e6dac42d881b435b95b50c/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/4a9ec66fd89cc55521e6dac42d881b435b95b50c)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ MEDIUM: tools: use the hashed random pair for UUID generation ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/85003563c5bbadd3f1197fb3f2801abb933566e3 \"MEDIUM: tools: use the hashed random pair for UUID generation\n\nThe UUID generation used to emit the internal PRNG state, which allows\nto predict previous and next ones, or disclose the internal PRNG state.\nWhile not critical, it may eventually become an issue.\n\nThis patch uses the new ha_random64_pair_hashed\\(\\) function that returns\na pair of u64 that are hashed from the internal PRNG state. It's almost\ntwice as fast on 20 threads \\(14.1M UUID/s vs 7.8M/s\\).\")\n\nShow description for 8500356 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on May 26 \n\n[ 8500356  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/85003563c5bbadd3f1197fb3f2801abb933566e3)\n\nCopy full SHA for 8500356 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/85003563c5bbadd3f1197fb3f2801abb933566e3/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/85003563c5bbadd3f1197fb3f2801abb933566e3)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ MINOR: tools: provide a function to generate a hashed random pair ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/26c3b3f41d37f058f358565fd8c6c84823be18f1 \"MINOR: tools: provide a function to generate a hashed random pair\n\nA lot of places call two ha_random64\\(\\) in a row to generate a 128-bit\nrandom. While it's now safe against linear analysis thanks to the XXH64\ncall, it's still particularly expensive due to the lock.\n\nHere we introduce a new function ha_random64_pair_hashed\\(\\), that feeds\ntwo uint64_t with a hash of the PRNG's internal state, and make it\nadvance. This will cut in half the number of calls to ha_random64\\(\\)\nand should recover a part of the performance lost in the lock. For\nnow it's not used.\")\n\nShow description for 26c3b3f \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on May 26 \n\n[ 26c3b3f  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/26c3b3f41d37f058f358565fd8c6c84823be18f1)\n\nCopy full SHA for 26c3b3f \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/26c3b3f41d37f058f358565fd8c6c84823be18f1/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/26c3b3f41d37f058f358565fd8c6c84823be18f1)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ BUG/MEDIUM: tools: insert an XXH64 layer on the PRNG output ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/9b6389c8a007cd86ebd61f1d3b33c13468abf26d \"BUG/MEDIUM: tools: insert an XXH64 layer on the PRNG output\n\nConsuming randoms in pairs directly exposes the internal PRNG's state\non moderately idle system. It can allow to predict next \\(or previous\\)\nUUIDs, QUIC retry tokens, and WS keys for example. Let's insert an XXH64\ncall on the ha_random64\\(\\) output to avoid this. We expand the boot seed\nas the secret at boot, and use now_ns as the seed for each call. The\noriginal ha_random64\\(\\) function was renamed to ha_random64_internal\\(\\)\nfor use cases where it's not a problem to directly use the internal\nstate.\n\nThe performance loss is only measurable when single-threaded. It drops\nfrom 7.32M UUID per second to 7.16M. Above that there is no longer any\ndifference due to the DWCAS loop which reaches up to 98.5% CPU at 20\nthreads.\n\nThis will need to be backported to stable releases after a period of\nobservation.\")\n\nShow description for 9b6389c \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on May 26 \n\n[ 9b6389c  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/9b6389c8a007cd86ebd61f1d3b33c13468abf26d)\n\nCopy full SHA for 9b6389c \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/9b6389c8a007cd86ebd61f1d3b33c13468abf26d/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/9b6389c8a007cd86ebd61f1d3b33c13468abf26d)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on May 11, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ BUG/MINOR: tools: fix memory leak in env_expand() error path ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/0995c914bd6406264e24b44278bbc806c43ba67c \"BUG/MINOR: tools: fix memory leak in env_expand\\(\\) error path\n\nWhen my_realloc2\\(\\) fails in env_expand\\(\\), the code jumps to 'leave:' and\nreturns NULL, but the original input 'in' is never freed \\(it's only freed\nat line 4919 in the success case\\). Given that callers typically pass it\nthe direct return of strdup\\(\\), it looks like it is expected to always be\nfreed. This can be backported everywhere.\")\n\nShow description for 0995c91 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on May 11 \n\n[ 0995c91  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/0995c914bd6406264e24b44278bbc806c43ba67c)\n\nCopy full SHA for 0995c91 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/0995c914bd6406264e24b44278bbc806c43ba67c/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/0995c914bd6406264e24b44278bbc806c43ba67c)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on May 7, 2026 \n\n  * ####  [ MEDIUM: tools: read_line_to_trash() handle empty files without \\n ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/83e6ae3334cbab6761b9c6c425b16db1e86d028a \"MEDIUM: tools: read_line_to_trash\\(\\) handle empty files without \\\\n\n\nfgets\\(\\) returns NULL when EOF is reached before newline, handle\nthat as a success for consistency, current behaviour is arguably a bug,\nthe API of fgets\\(\\) is pretty weird after all so someone probably forgot.\")\n\nShow description for 83e6ae3 \n\n[ kanashimia ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=kanashimia)\n\nauthored and \n\n[ wlallemand ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wlallemand)\n\ncommitted  on May 7 \n\n[ 83e6ae3  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/83e6ae3334cbab6761b9c6c425b16db1e86d028a)\n\nCopy full SHA for 83e6ae3 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/h