t/c0bf395cdee1fd11e9246a410dd39621bb5c0685)\n\nCopy full SHA for c0bf395 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/c0bf395cdee1fd11e9246a410dd39621bb5c0685/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/c0bf395cdee1fd11e9246a410dd39621bb5c0685)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ MINOR: connection: track mux calls to report their allocation context ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/ec7b07b65045a0f1a8e7ca735d29562e79bfb1c6 \"MINOR: connection: track mux calls to report their allocation context\n\nMost calls to mux ops were instrumented with a CALL_MUX_WITH_RET\\(\\) or\nCALL_MUX_NO_RET\\(\\) macro in order to make the current thread's context\npoint to the called mux and be able to track its allocations. Only\na bunch of harmless mux_ctl\\(\\) and ->subscribe/unsubscribe calls were\nleft untouched since useless. But destroy/detach/shut/init/snd_buf\nand rcv_buf are now tracked.\n\nIt will not show allocations performed in IO callback via tasklet\nwakeups however.\n\nIn order to ease reading of the output, cmp_memprof_ctx\\(\\) knows about\nmuxes and sorts based on the .subscribe function address instead of\nthe mux_ops address so as to keep various callers grouped.\")\n\nShow description for ec7b07b \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Mar 12 \n\n[ ec7b07b  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/ec7b07b65045a0f1a8e7ca735d29562e79bfb1c6)\n\nCopy full SHA for ec7b07b \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/ec7b07b65045a0f1a8e7ca735d29562e79bfb1c6/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/ec7b07b65045a0f1a8e7ca735d29562e79bfb1c6)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ MINOR: filters: set the exec context to the current filter config ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/3fb8659d045fe972b3a38fd1108a07fe3a55bf3a \"MINOR: filters: set the exec context to the current filter config\n\nDoing this allows to report the allocations/releases performed by filters\nwhen running with memory profiling enabled. The flt_conf pointer is kept\nand the report shows the filter name.\")\n\nShow description for 3fb8659 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Mar 12 \n\n[ 3fb8659  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/3fb8659d045fe972b3a38fd1108a07fe3a55bf3a)\n\nCopy full SHA for 3fb8659 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/3fb8659d045fe972b3a38fd1108a07fe3a55bf3a/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/3fb8659d045fe972b3a38fd1108a07fe3a55bf3a)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ MINOR: actions: also report execution contexts registered directly ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/43b56c22c70b2af7bfcafd884ebacf88acd3b2a1 \"MINOR: actions: also report execution contexts registered directly\n\nThis now reports directly registered actions using new type\nTH_EX_CTX_ACTION which will report the first keyword of the\nlist.\")\n\nShow description for 43b56c2 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/commits?author=wtarreau)\n\ncommitted  on Mar 12 \n\n[ 43b56c2  ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/43b56c22c70b2af7bfcafd884ebacf88acd3b2a1)\n\nCopy full SHA for 43b56c2 \n\n[ ](/haproxy/haproxy/blob/43b56c22c70b2af7bfcafd884ebacf88acd3b2a1/src/tools.c) [ ](/haproxy/haproxy/tree/43b56c22c70b2af7bfcafd884ebacf88acd3b2a1)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ MINOR: tools: support an execution context that is just a function ](/haproxy/haproxy/commit/261cae3b6d5625c98c4677840e1c19c476cb492a \"MINOR: tools: support an execution context that is just a function\n\nThe purpose here is to be able to spot certain callbacks, such as the\nSSL message callbacks, which are difficult to associate to anything.\nThus we introduce a new context type, TH_EX_CTX_FUNC, for which the\ncontext is just the function pointed to by the void *pointer. One\ndifficulty with callbacks is that the allocation and release contexts\nwill likely be different, so the code should be properly structured\nto allow proper tracking, either by instrumenting all calls, or by\nmaking sure that the free calls are easy to spot in a report.\")\n\nShow description for 261cae3 \n\n[ ](/wtarreau) [ wtarreau ](/haproxy/haproxy/